      "text": "To determine the possible degrees of the remainder when a polynomial \\( P(x) \\) is divided by \\( 2x^2 - 7x + 18 \\), we will use the Polynomial Division Algorithm. The division algorithm states that for any polynomials \\( P(x) \\) and \\( D(x) \\) where the degree of \\( D(x) \\) is less than the degree of \\( P(x) \\), we can write:\n\n\\[\nP(x) = (2x^2 - 7x + 18)Q(x) + R(x)\n\\]\n\nwhere \\( Q(x) \\) is the quotient and \\( R(x) \\) is the remainder. The degree of the remainder \\( R(x) \\) must be less than the degree of the divisor \\( 2x^2 - 7x + 18 \\). Since the degree of \\( 2x^2 - 7x + 18 \\) is 2, the degree of the remainder \\( R(x) \\) must be less than 2.\n\nTherefore, the possible degrees of the remainder are 0 and 1. We can express these as:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{0, 1}\n\\]",
